1
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:10,410
The End

2
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:11,510
Too bad.

3
00:00:11,593 --> 00:00:12,800
Looks like I win again.

4
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,497
Hoorah, hoorah, hoorah, hoorah, hoorah.

5
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:16,757
Hard at work, I see.

6
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,780
Hand over the keys to the cells.

7
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:21,610
Huh?

8
00:00:21,693 --> 00:00:22,523
Who the hell are you?

9
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:28,610
Really?

10
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,862
Seems your manners are as
foul as your body odor.

11
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:46,620
What did you say?

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,360
You've got a lot of nerve, little lady.

13
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:53,144
I could say the same about you.

14
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,971
Let's fix that, shall we?

15
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,260
Now, kneel before me!

16
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:05,450
Negative...

17
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:06,363
HOME!

18
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:08,790
Negative!

19
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,230
Negative!

20
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,670
Negative!

21
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,904
I'm not even fit to be a
worm on a fishing hook.

22
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:29,379
I'm gonna crawl into one of these
prison cells just to hide my shame.

23
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:37,500
Thank you, boys.

24
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,680
All right, let's go.

25
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,900
Not very lively in here, is it?

26
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,100
Hey, stop that! Huh?

27
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:23,520
Call, get up!

28
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,390
I know you.

29
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:36,200
Wait a second, you're Koby the hero!

30
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:42,400
I'll unlock this door
for you, and in return,

31
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:45,738
you'll free Master Moria
from his cell deeper inside.

32
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:47,590
Moria?

33
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,380
Gecko Moria is being held here?

34
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:55,637
Wait, are you telling me you want me
to help a notorious criminal escape?

35
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:56,940
I am, yes.

36
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:00,121
Because if you don't, then
he'll surely be killed.

37
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:06,420
How can I set him free?

38
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:11,380
All of us are Sting Stingers!

39
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,217
All of us

40
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:19,917
are Stingers!

41
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,377
The end of the day, the end of the day.

42
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:24,657
I want to go to the same place.

43
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:27,177
But it's one thing that shines.

44
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:31,280
The legends are coming up with me.

45
00:04:19,553 --> 00:04:20,383
I don't have to end my life.

46
00:04:20,466 --> 00:04:21,296
I don't have fun.

47
00:04:21,379 --> 00:04:22,209
Zubyaya.

48
00:04:22,292 --> 00:04:23,122
The loudest of the word.

49
00:04:23,205 --> 00:04:24,035
Is my heart.

50
00:04:24,118 --> 00:04:24,948
That's all about.

51
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:25,861
If the word is sent.

52
00:04:25,944 --> 00:04:26,774
Then, these people will forget.

53
00:04:26,857 --> 00:04:27,687
I love you. We are with you.

54
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:28,600
We are in the world.

55
00:04:28,683 --> 00:04:29,513
We are still keeping them.

56
00:04:29,596 --> 00:04:31,060
Let the world start?

57
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,440
We got some big news!

58
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,329
Captain Covey has escaped!

59
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:46,740
Are you serious?

60
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,420
Oh, yeah!

61
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:52,877
If he's free, the Commodore can't
stop us from going after him.

62
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:55,557
We'll be set for life if
we can catch him ourselves.

63
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,297
Then what the hell are we waiting for?

64
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:00,968
All right, he's already got a
bounty, so we'll be good to go!

65
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:03,377
All we gotta do is take
a cent at Crosskill.

66
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,290
Hell yeah!

67
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:08,297
I bought odds on him with a win
ticket, and the payout's gonna be huge!

68
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:10,477
How much will we get if we kill him?

69
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,877
You might want to sit down for this one.

70
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:15,360
His bounty is five stars!

71
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,917
That means he's worth
five treasure chests!

72
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,740
Five hundred million berries!

73
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:22,797
Captains are usually only worth one star!

74
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,840
They must really want
this guy dead, huh? Yeah!

75
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,500
All right, men!

76
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:30,920
The hunt is on!

77
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:33,480
We're about to hit the jackpots!

78
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,940
I've got an itch on the
left side of my chest.

79
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,562
That's where the slaves
are held before the sale.

80
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:49,660
Are you kidding me?

81
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:50,900
They're escaping!

82
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,300
The slaves are running for it?

83
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,710
No!

84
00:05:54,793 --> 00:05:56,297
That means we can hunt them down!

85
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:57,210
Oh boy!

86
00:05:57,293 --> 00:05:58,749
Don't even think about it!

87
00:05:58,880 --> 00:05:59,997
Keep your claws in check!

88
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,760
Bring him back, now!

89
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:06,200
And you better not kill Koby, or
I'll make sure you answer to teach!

90
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:11,600
Wait, did that rock? Just talk? No.

91
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,277
Pizzotto knows we're here.

92
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,500
We need to run!

93
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,040
We're not gonna make it.

94
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,580
Please, Koby.

95
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,917
You need to get out of
here while you still can.

96
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,457
Don't let us slow you down.

97
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:28,277
I promised that I'd help you escape.

98
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:31,060
And you will, by using me as bait.

99
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:36,340
Run as fast as you can, and no matter
what, don't let the pirates catch you. Go!

100
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,120
I'll see you all again soon!

101
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,000
Thank you, Captain Kobe!

102
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,840
You're a living saint!

103
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:04,380
Why don't you capture the
damn slaves yourself, Pizarro?

104
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,294
Because I don't want Teach
to come back and chew me out.

105
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:19,594
Whenever I move too much, I end up
breaking things, and it's a huge mess.

106
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,200
Why don't I stop him, huh?

107
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,137
Forget it, Bazooka.

108
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:28,760
What are you gonna do?

109
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:38,587
If I set the town on fire, they'll
have nowhere to run, right?

110
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:52,117
That would be a complete catastrophe!

111
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,082
Don't you dare!

112
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,177
Teach is gonna be Furious!

113
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:56,880
Uh, what's that?

114
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,099
Burn him, you say?

115
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:00,840
Absolutely no burning anyone, you hear me?

116
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:03,300
We just finished repairing Rocky Port.

117
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,560
All right, have it your way.

118
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,200
We'll let Wolf handle it.

119
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,960
Wait. Wolf?

120
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,860
That's the worst idea I've ever heard.

121
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,747
He'll crush the whole
town into kitty litter.

122
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:25,540
Over here!

123
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,757
Damn it, what am I supposed to do now?

124
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:33,840
I can't keep running away forever.

125
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,020
I'll be okay.

126
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:40,857
I just have to hold out until
the others can get out of here.

127
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,058
I'll figure out the rest after that.

128
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,460
Over here.

129
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:56,037
I'm so glad you're here
Kobe cuz I've got big

130
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:59,857
plans I'm gonna turn pirate

131
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:03,557
island into a full-flex

132
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:08,797
country one that flies the
flag of the world government

133
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:14,800
that'll make me a king of
the blackbeard kingtown

134
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,640
So what do you think?

135
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,577
I think your plan's as
ridiculous as you are.

136
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:24,977
You really think the
government would agree to that?

137
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:27,060
To a country made up of criminals?

138
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:28,410
Hey!

139
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:31,657
Don't you know it's rude to
stomp on someone's dream?

140
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:35,505
They might see it my way, now
I've got you as a bargaining chip!

141
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:40,974
The day the Navy negotiates with
terrorists will be the day justice dies!

142
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,600
And I won't be your bargaining chip.

143
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,660
I can't be.

144
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,285
I'm a member of S .W .O .R .D.

145
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:51,437
The hell is S .W .O .R .D.?

146
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,640
Never heard of it.

147
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,380
So that's how it is.

148
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,240
This will not end well.

149
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:59,257
Call off the trade, Teach.

150
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,600
It won't work. Huh?

151
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:12,302
Since this kid's from S .W .O .R .D., that
means he's a Marine, but not officially.

152
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:15,820
Sword members surrender their navy code.

153
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,680
They aren't like their comrades.

154
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:23,177
They're marines who have
submitted their resignations.

155
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:27,297
They can pick fights with the four
emperors without permission from above.

156
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:31,674
They can also disregard orders at
their discretion and move as they like.

157
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,480
And that's the issue.

158
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:39,437
The navy is absolved of all
responsibility for their actions.

159
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:42,780
They can cut them loose as they see fit.

160
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,080
Ain't that cute?

161
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:51,197
Most breeds just sit on their asses
waiting for Daddy's permission to fight us.

162
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:54,280
But you do what you like,
consequences be damned!

163
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,300
I get it now!

164
00:10:58,540 --> 00:10:59,680
I like your style!

165
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:04,140
That said, I'm not gonna change my plan.

166
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:07,200
Cause you're a special case.

167
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,700
It doesn't matter if
you're with Zorn or not.

168
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:14,200
The public won't like it
if the Navy abandons you.

169
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:18,100
It's bad press to turn
your back on a hero, right?

170
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:21,080
Your life's in the people's hands.

171
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:25,940
Looks like the world government
will lose credibility either way.

172
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:31,800
I think he gets the
message. We're done here.

173
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,400
Lock him up.

174
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,620
And don't let him escape!

175
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:41,040
Get back here, Koby!

176
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:48,721
Here's the deal.

177
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,940
I'll unlock this door
for you, and in return,

178
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:55,278
you'll free Master Moria
from his cell deeper inside.

179
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:58,577
Guess this is what I deserve
for helping a pirate.

180
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,600
But necessity knows no law!

181
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:07,210
Huh?

182
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,620
The hell's that?

183
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,760
Three Marines just showed up at the port!

184
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:25,080
Huh? Marines? That can't be.

185
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,710
Hurry up!

186
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,200
They're strong! Be careful!

187
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,240
Did someone come to rescue me?

188
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,840
No, stop it, Kobe.

189
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,757
This is not the time for your selfishness.

190
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,075
What's wrong with me?

191
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,560
Who are they? They're monsters!

192
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:03,277
Looks like they're heading
straight to the center of town!

193
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,657
What do they want from us?

194
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:06,480
I don't know! Just shoot!

195
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:15,510
What?

196
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:17,160
They didn't even flinch!

197
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:20,800
End of the line, monster!

198
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,650
Whoa!

199
00:13:24,733 --> 00:13:25,740
His head came off!

200
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:29,160
Woo-hoo!

201
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,480
You see that?

202
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,875
That's how it's done!

203
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:34,000
They're not so tough now!

204
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,720
That hurts.

205
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,980
He's a Lokiotype!

206
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,242
What the hell is wrong with him?

207
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,880
His body's like clay!

208
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:50,960
Where are you, Koby?

209
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,200
Hey, look over there.

210
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:58,837
I swear I just saw those
buildings move on their own.

211
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,391
Yeah, sure they did, pal.

212
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:02,736
How's quitting drinking going for ya?

213
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:12,180
Be good and do as I say.

214
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,777
Now march forward!

215
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,920
Is she whipping that building?

216
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,030
That's weird.

217
00:14:20,113 --> 00:14:20,997
Come on!

218
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,340
Where's your stamina?

219
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:27,500
Is that really the best you can do?

220
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,237
You are so pathetic.

221
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:32,202
I kind of feel like I
shouldn't be watching this!

222
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,357
Hi boys.

223
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,397
Finish staring.

224
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:37,057
We are.

225
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:38,097
Wait?

226
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:39,420
That mark!

227
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:49,740
You pirates act like you've
never seen a marine before.

228
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,840
How adorable.

229
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,820
Come here.

230
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:06,420
Let me teach you a lesson.

231
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,060
What now?

232
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:18,440
I'm done for!

233
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:24,980
Eyes on the target, boys!

234
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:31,380
Ready, aim, fire!

235
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:45,160
Huh?

236
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,640
What? What?

237
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,560
What?

238
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,300
Oh my! How lovely!

239
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,720
Wait no!

240
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:04,897
What is this?

241
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:08,140
Where are these goddamn
flowers coming from?

242
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,160
Wait, I've seen this.

243
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,460
Of course!

244
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:16,730
Dr.

245
00:16:16,813 --> 00:16:18,200
Vegapunk invented this!

246
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:25,460
In fact, it earned him
the Mobile Peace Prize!

247
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,800
Nobody cares about that, okay?

248
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,700
Who the hell picked this two our guns?

249
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:32,860
Hey, Kobe!

250
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,184
Come here and stay close to me!

251
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:41,000
But not in a weird way!

252
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:46,300
Wait, Heibati?

253
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,872
What are you doing here?

254
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,520
Are those... That's right.

255
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:51,937
They're flower rounds.

256
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:53,057
But they won't last.

257
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:54,140
We have to hurry!

258
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:58,658
We need to go before the enemy's
gunpowder stops turning into flowers!

259
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:01,277
Also, I, uh...

260
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,157
I don't want your food to get cold.

261
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,757
Because I...

262
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:05,717
I...

263
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,580
I packed you a lunch. Huh?

264
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,640
No, I miss Walk!

265
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:12,152
I mean, you misheard me!

266
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:18,590
Goalik!

267
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,280
Prince, what's the status?

268
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,180
We're in the clear.

269
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,838
Everything went off without a hitch.

270
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,760
Colby's doing fine.

271
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,477
Wait a sec!

272
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,037
This place doesn't look right?

273
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,040
Where are we?

274
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:43,650
Hey!

275
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:44,920
Everyone look!

276
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,840
That building just moved!

277
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:48,210
No way!

278
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,720
It's too late They moved the
buildings and trapped us here.

279
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,901
All right, whenever you're ready.

280
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,732
Aim for the dead center.

281
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:02,098
I just got confirmation from Prince.

282
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:03,832
Everyone is in position.

283
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,549
We're ready, Vice Admiral.

284
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,400
Everyone, hang on tight!

285
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,100
To hell we go! Whoa!

286
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,350
Ha-ha!

287
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,740
OK, hurry!

288
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,940
If you're ready, I am too.

289
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,540
Whoa, what the hell is that?

290
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:31,637
I'm not sticking around to find out.

291
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:32,560
Look up!

292
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,744
There's a baby ship in the sky!

293
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,660
It's flying straight for us!

294
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,080
But why? And how?

295
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:55,400
Whose ship is that?

296
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,400
Oh, looks like it's falling.

297
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:01,660
We gotta go! Run away!

298
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:06,900
No way!

299
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,400
I know that ship!

300
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,160
No, that can't be right!

301
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,675
I thought he retired!

302
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,640
The legendary hero!

303
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:17,920
He's coming!

304
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:26,380
It's Vice Admiral Couran!

305
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:28,530
Koby!

306
00:19:28,613 --> 00:19:30,400
I came to get you, boy!

307
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,300
Come on!

308
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,760
We have to take cover! Whip's red!

309
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,711
Take the way out of here!

310
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:42,170
What?

311
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,000
You want a piece of me?

312
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,700
I'm not worth any of this.

313
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:12,440
You would risk starting
a war just to protect me?

314
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:15,480
Hey, morons!

315
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,877
Who do you think you kidnapped?

316
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:20,260
Do you know who the kid is?

317
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:31,660
Kobe's not just the future of the Navy!

318
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:38,840
That boy is my favorite student!

319
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:43,280
Policy!

320
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,640
IMPACT!

321
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:01,500
Kill me alone, Marcus!

322
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,640
My back! Damn, Garp!

323
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:17,740
He's insane!

324
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:19,920
Where'd you go? Your deck!

325
00:22:20,340 --> 00:22:21,220
Hey, pirates!

326
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:22,400
Not so fast!

327
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:26,600
We've got plenty more
firepower where that came from!

328
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:36,460
Still a few buildings left.

329
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:38,980
I must be losing my touch.

330
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:40,977
Losing your touch?

331
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:43,460
Quit rubbing it in, you old bastard!

332
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:45,600
Vice Admiral Garp!

333
00:22:47,820 --> 00:22:49,420
Hey, there he is!

334
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:51,180
You all right, Kobe?

335
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:55,520
I'm so happy!

336
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,920
I thought my body was gonna die!

337
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:01,240
And once again, Garp overdid it.

338
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:03,480
Such a naughty boy, isn't he?

339
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:08,100
I can't believe he said Kobe is
the future of the Navy. As if.

340
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:10,217
I'll put that kid in his place.

341
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:12,880
I know you're too spoiled to know better,

342
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:16,314
but that's not the sort of
thing you should say out loud

343
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:28,237
Pashigi even people who
are from sword are here.

344
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:29,150
Hmm.

345
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,927
What have you got there
a big ball and chain?

346
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:35,720
We had no choice

347
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:41,680
Something!

348
00:23:42,140 --> 00:23:43,360
We can't!

349
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:51,640
He-body!

350
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:53,220
He-body!

351
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:57,720
She's frozen solid!

352
00:24:08,140 --> 00:24:08,970
What?!

353
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:11,190
Kuzan...

354
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:12,780
Why, Kuzan?

355
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:15,257
Why are you doing this?!

356
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:20,100
Hunt Freezybody right now!
Woo-hoo! Hell yeah! It's Apigi!

357
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:23,540
You guys are dead now!

358
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,420
Go, Koza!

359
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:29,426
Don't get me in trouble, kid.

360
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:31,167
Can't have you getting away.

361
00:24:31,540 --> 00:24:33,260
How would that look to teach?

362
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:35,960
Two years ago,

363
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,997
there was a struggle
to determine who would

364
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:40,837
be the next fleet admiral
at Navy headquarters.

365
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:46,880
To that end, Admiral Aka 'inu
and Admiral Alkechi had a duel.

366
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:55,777
The fight went on for ten days
before a victor was decided.

367
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:58,820
Akainu stood triumphant.

368
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:04,700
Regardless, Alkeji refused to serve
under Akainu as Fleet Admiral,

369
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:07,600
and so he resigned.

370
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,300
What the hell?

371
00:25:28,700 --> 00:25:30,300
Black man is here!

372
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:33,277
Come on, get out of
town while you're down!

373
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:34,190
Hey!

374
00:25:34,273 --> 00:25:37,060
What is this? What happened here? Stop!

375
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:39,560
Someone tell me who did this!

376
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:44,350
Wait.

377
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:46,260
I know what this is.

378
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:49,260
I don't even gotta ask.

379
00:25:49,740 --> 00:25:53,152
There's only one guy in the
world who could pull this off.

380
00:25:54,700 --> 00:25:56,140
I thought so.

381
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:57,910
Aokiji.

382
00:26:10,600 --> 00:26:12,117
What's the big idea?

383
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,017
Turning my crew into ice cubes.

384
00:26:14,100 --> 00:26:14,980
Fix it.

385
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:17,980
Why don't you fix your attitude?

386
00:26:20,660 --> 00:26:22,500
Wouldn't do that if I were you.

387
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:25,940
Your friends will shatter and die.

388
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:31,280
Come on now, you think
I started this fight?

389
00:26:32,380 --> 00:26:35,120
You know what kind of company you keep.

390
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:39,000
Also, I'm sure you
heard the news about me.

391
00:26:39,700 --> 00:26:41,520
I'm in a state of mourning.

392
00:26:41,980 --> 00:26:43,640
You shouldn't test me.

393
00:26:45,220 --> 00:26:48,560
So let's cool it with
the demands, shall we?

394
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:15,120
Who's ready for more bombs?

395
00:27:16,900 --> 00:27:19,660
Damn, Freezer Fingers,
you sure can't drink!

396
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:22,380
You're not so bad yourself, shitbag.

397
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:28,300
Okay, before the battle,
what does Akainu say?

398
00:27:31,460 --> 00:27:33,320
We climbed the ranks together.

399
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:34,957
Now we fight to the death.

400
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:37,700
I'm starting to feel a
hot lump in my throat.

401
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:39,600
That's what he said.

402
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,586
And you know what I told him?

403
00:27:42,260 --> 00:27:44,820
No shit, asshole, you're made of magma.

404
00:27:47,080 --> 00:27:48,940
Look what that bastard did.

405
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:55,797
Took off my whole damn leg So that's what

406
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,317
happens when two admirals
decide to throw down,

407
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:59,230
huh?

408
00:27:59,313 --> 00:28:00,545
So'd you pay him back or what?

409
00:28:00,660 --> 00:28:02,680
Rip off one of his arms, maybe?

410
00:28:03,380 --> 00:28:04,210
Nah.

411
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:09,300
But he's got some scars to remember me by!

412
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:13,857
That reminds me, Commodore.

413
00:28:13,940 --> 00:28:16,417
He might know the man with the burn scar.

414
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:17,440
The what?

415
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:18,817
Who the hell's that?

416
00:28:18,900 --> 00:28:21,960
The deal is, if we want
to make it to Laugh Tale,

417
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:24,394
we gotta find the Four Road Poneglyphs.

418
00:28:26,260 --> 00:28:29,672
You know them when you see
them, cause they're bright red.

419
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:32,020
Kaido and Big Mom have one each.

420
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:34,900
But what about the other two?

421
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,000
They're still a mystery.

422
00:28:37,480 --> 00:28:41,140
We're just hoping fate will
guide us to them. That's right.

423
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:43,760
Well, we do have one tiny lead.

424
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:46,999
We heard some man with the
Burnscar has one of them.

425
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:51,040
You mean me? No, not you!

426
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,082
You just got that the other day!

427
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,760
What the mystery, no.

428
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:10,320
Rumor has it that the man with the
burn scar sails on a pitch black ship.

429
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:20,980
But if anyone approaches it,
their ship will be whisked away,

430
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:23,960
swallowed up by a giant whirlpool.

431
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:30,266
I'd assume the fellow
has a Devil Fruit power.

432
00:29:31,020 --> 00:29:34,255
Just a hunch, but I bet the
guy is with the government.

433
00:29:35,100 --> 00:29:38,317
They've got their hands in everything
and plenty of dark secrets.

434
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:41,120
They know everyone needs those stones.

435
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:46,200
If they had one, all they'd have to
do is hold on to it, and we'd be sunk.

436
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:50,280
No pirate could find their way
to Laugh Tale or the One Piece.

437
00:29:52,380 --> 00:29:53,640
The Poneglyphs, huh?

438
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,277
Brings back memories.

439
00:29:55,360 --> 00:29:56,772
Hate to break it to you,

440
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:00,889
but I never saw a giant
red stone in Ohara.

441
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:02,077
I'd remember.

442
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:05,917
I haven't forgotten a thing
About that day the day I

443
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,897
watched my best friend rebel
against the government and

444
00:30:08,980 --> 00:30:12,637
the day that I Saw those sad
eyes when I held that poor

445
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:19,340
lonely girl's fate in my
hands that story sounds boring

446
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:28,397
Commodore what should we do a power
like his could be quite useful

447
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:30,757
I say we take it while his Guards down

448
00:30:30,840 --> 00:30:37,840
come

449
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:42,557
on then

450
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:43,470
you want to know

451
00:30:43,553 --> 00:30:45,277
what it feels like to freeze the

452
00:30:45,360 --> 00:30:52,017
Death take it easy buddy so the

453
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:57,980
rumors are true you're hunting people with
strong Devil Fruit powers, aren't you?

454
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:02,000
Then try to take mine, I dare you!

455
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:07,600
Whoa, whoa!

456
00:31:08,500 --> 00:31:09,640
Listen to me!

457
00:31:09,880 --> 00:31:12,877
My crew members are getting
carried away, that's all.

458
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:15,500
Let me apologize on their behalf.

459
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:17,780
I don't want to steal your power.

460
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:20,160
I want you to join my crew.

461
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:24,317
Are you nuts, an ex-Marine?

462
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:25,300
Why not?

463
00:31:25,540 --> 00:31:27,364
You're out of a job now, right?

464
00:31:27,680 --> 00:31:29,160
You got any place to go?

465
00:31:29,360 --> 00:31:31,184
Anything you're planning to do?

466
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:33,871
Not going to be defending justice anymore.

467
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,842
Guess I've sunk pretty low, huh?

468
00:31:37,280 --> 00:31:40,957
A good-for-nothing pirate's worried
about the state of my employment.

469
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:43,840
Men like us will find
trouble anywhere we go.

470
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:47,704
Can't run, so you might
as well face it head on.

471
00:31:47,980 --> 00:31:49,580
What flag will you fly?

472
00:31:49,860 --> 00:31:53,077
When you put your life on the line,
what will you be fighting for?

473
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:53,990
Tell me!

474
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,577
I've got my own brand
of justice my own code

475
00:31:58,660 --> 00:32:01,837
this won't be nothing like
the navy i promise you.

476
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:05,077
Yeah i'm sure but i'll still
get stabbed straight in the back

477
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:08,037
you think sharing a couple of
drinks means i can trust you?

478
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:11,897
Of course not i don't think you
understand how pirates work.

479
00:32:11,980 --> 00:32:16,200
We're not here to make friends we're
a crew but we're not buddy buddy.

480
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:23,560
We all have a common goal.

481
00:32:26,180 --> 00:32:29,200
All pirates need is an
alignment of interests.

482
00:32:33,300 --> 00:32:35,180
You're free now, Kuzan.

483
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:36,320
Your choice.

484
00:32:37,780 --> 00:32:39,700
What do you really want?

485
00:32:54,460 --> 00:32:56,160
Stop this, Kuzan!

486
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:58,480
Fahibari out right now!

487
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:00,780
Let Kobe escape from here!

488
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:02,860
Come back to the Navy!

489
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:07,940
You never change, huh?

490
00:33:08,100 --> 00:33:10,900
Can't stop to think you'd
just run your mouth.

491
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:17,717
But I'm afraid I can't
help you today, Garp.

492
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:19,080
I'm sorry.

493
00:33:20,020 --> 00:33:21,977
You've always been straightforward.

494
00:33:22,060 --> 00:33:24,117
I admire that.

495
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:26,537
You inspired me.

496
00:33:26,620 --> 00:33:29,140
So I'm living the way I want to now.

497
00:33:34,460 --> 00:33:36,180
You damn fool.

498
00:33:52,220 --> 00:33:54,100
Ice-Ball!

499
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:03,420
Vice Admiral Garp!

500
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:06,960
Vice Admiral!

501
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:13,780
Your old student and your new student.

502
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:18,220
Would you do anything to save
Kobe, even if it kills me?

503
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:22,980
What are you doing bringing up the past?

504
00:34:24,180 --> 00:34:27,000
I taught you to live
in a moment, didn't I?

505
00:34:31,680 --> 00:34:34,020
How the hell did he break free?

506
00:34:53,580 --> 00:34:55,900
Here's another lesson.

507
00:35:18,660 --> 00:35:24,380
Men who waver are weak!

508
00:35:25,800 --> 00:35:29,360
Come on, Blue Holes!

509
00:35:59,100 --> 00:36:01,900
Meanwhile, on the coast
of Winner Island...

510
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:12,100
Ugh.

511
00:36:14,100 --> 00:36:15,900
He-he-he-he-he.

512
00:36:39,240 --> 00:36:41,637
Now that your ship is
out of the picture you

513
00:36:41,720 --> 00:36:43,637
haven't just lost your
right to call yourself.

514
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:49,277
A pirate you lost your
only escape you stole 100

515
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:51,997
hearts that day at Rocky
Port you had to expect

516
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:55,397
some kind of payback from
me those poor pirates

517
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:58,360
back at my base living
every damn day in fear.

518
00:36:59,100 --> 00:37:01,937
So I think I'll bring it
back to your heart as a gift.

519
00:37:02,020 --> 00:37:05,360
Bet that'll have the sad
bastard Chop it for joy.

520
00:37:12,240 --> 00:37:14,420
Oh wow, you made this for me?

521
00:37:14,680 --> 00:37:18,680
But I haven't been able to test it,
so I can't guarantee it'll work.

522
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:25,597
Let me think.

523
00:37:25,680 --> 00:37:29,800
We could sell your fruit, but I
think I could put it to better use.

524
00:37:30,320 --> 00:37:33,520
They say it can grant
someone eternal life, right?

525
00:37:41,420 --> 00:37:42,250
Shoot!

526
00:37:42,800 --> 00:37:43,960
Stay away!

527
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:46,510
Huh?

528
00:37:46,593 --> 00:37:48,100
That's my captain!

529
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:07,600
It can't be so long, but how?

530
00:38:07,820 --> 00:38:09,232
The moon isn't even out!

531
00:38:25,680 --> 00:38:26,510
Ah!

532
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,230
Captain!

533
00:38:59,700 --> 00:39:00,780
Damn it!

534
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:02,449
They're headed to the sea!

535
00:39:02,580 --> 00:39:03,900
Get them now!

536
00:39:11,540 --> 00:39:13,540
Take me back, Beppo.

537
00:39:18,380 --> 00:39:19,940
They're my friends.

538
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,540
I can't leave them.

539
00:39:22,820 --> 00:39:24,057
I'm sorry, Captain!

540
00:39:24,140 --> 00:39:26,080
We can't risk it.

541
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:29,660
But your crew was forged in
the cold waters of the North.

542
00:39:32,260 --> 00:39:35,560
Have faith in them through every fight.

543
00:39:35,820 --> 00:39:37,100
They've held strong.

544
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:40,200
They won't die here.

545
00:39:46,560 --> 00:39:49,040
We've overcome so much together.

546
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:52,960
We have to survive.

547
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:55,840
All of us!

548
00:40:05,540 --> 00:40:07,200
Don't die, Captain!

549
00:40:07,940 --> 00:40:09,580
We need you!

550
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:20,180
The Bartlett-Winner Island in
the New World came to an end.

551
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:30,620
Blackbeard destroyed the Polar Tang,

552
00:40:30,940 --> 00:40:35,960
the submarine of the Heart
Pirates, and it sank into the sea.

553
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:44,660
The Heart Pirates, led by
Trafalgar Law, were defeated.

554
00:40:54,140 --> 00:40:59,220
Do you know how to run
away from the world?

555
00:41:00,020 --> 00:41:05,400
I don't know how to run away,
but I don't know how to run away.

556
00:41:07,140 --> 00:41:12,040
I'm still looking at my head in my head,

557
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:19,940
I'm still looking for the future.

558
00:41:49,940 --> 00:41:55,560
I'm laughing at you.

559
00:41:57,080 --> 00:42:00,500
I'm singing the same song.

560
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:05,657
If you're a big man,

561
00:42:05,740 --> 00:42:08,420
I don't want to forget.

562
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:12,614
I'm waiting for you to come to the end.
